Disables Jekyll on GitHub Pages.

Without this file Pages runs every push through Jekyll, which drops paths it
treats as build artefacts - `vendor/` among them - so index.html asks for
vendor/react-18.2.0.min.js and Pages serves a 404. The app then reports the
three libraries as missing from the upload, which is true of the SITE even
though the files were pushed to the repository.

It must sit next to index.html and be committed. An empty file is enough; this
text is here so nobody deletes it as clutter. See CONTRACT.md 11fl.
